<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="no" ?><library hasTree="1" revision="R2024b"><block_node SID="1" hasTree="0"><block_name>Control Algorithms</block_name><block_class></block_class><block_desc></block_desc><block_path>$bdroot/Control Algorithms</block_path><block_open>$bdroot/Control Algorithms</block_open><block_isNotLeafBlk>1</block_isNotLeafBlk><block_position>-185   65  -55  140</block_position><block_icon>Control@20@Algorithms.svg</block_icon><keywords></keywords><port_domains>NA.NA:0</port_domains><block_type>SubSystem</block_type><block_reference></block_reference><block_node SID="19" hasTree="0"><block_name>Vector Field Histogram</block_name><block_class>nav.slalgs.internal.VectorFieldHistogram</block_class><block_desc>Compute an obstacle-free steering direction using range sensor data in terms of ranges and angles, and a target direction. 

The ports Ranges and Angles accept vectors of the same length. The port TargetDir accepts a scalar angle in radians. The port SteerDir outputs an obstacle-free moving direction in radians.

The positive angles are measured counterclockwise with respect to vehicle's forward direction.</block_desc><block_path>$bdroot/Control Algorithms/Vector Field Histogram</block_path><block_open>$bdroot/Control Algorithms/Vector Field Histogram</block_open><block_isNotLeafBlk>0</block_isNotLeafBlk><block_position>185   82  325  158</block_position><block_icon>Control@20@Algorithms/Vector@20@Field@20@Histogram.svg</block_icon><keywords></keywords><port_domains>signal.in_signal:3,signal.out_signal:1</port_domains><block_type>MATLABSystem</block_type><block_reference>robotalgslib/Vector Field Histogram</block_reference></block_node><block_node SID="18" hasTree="0"><block_name>Pure Pursuit</block_name><block_class>nav.slalgs.internal.PurePursuit</block_class><block_desc>Compute linear and angular velocity control commands for following a path using a set of waypoints and the current pose of a differential drive robot.

The input port Pose accepts a three-element state vector of xy-positions and vehicle heading, [x y theta]. The input port Waypoints accepts an N-by-2 matrix as xy-coordinates. The output ports Linear Velocity and Angular Velocity return linear and angular velocities as scalar values, respectively. The Target Direction port outputs an angle with respect to the forward direction of the robot with positive angles measured counter-clockwise. 

Set the Lookahead distance to tune how closely the robot follows the path. A smaller Lookahead distance improves path tracking but can lead to instability.</block_desc><block_path>$bdroot/Control Algorithms/Pure Pursuit</block_path><block_open>$bdroot/Control Algorithms/Pure Pursuit</block_open><block_isNotLeafBlk>0</block_isNotLeafBlk><block_position>360   80  500  155</block_position><block_icon>Control@20@Algorithms/Pure@20@Pursuit.svg</block_icon><keywords></keywords><port_domains>signal.in_signal:2,signal.out_signal:2</port_domains><block_type>MATLABSystem</block_type><block_reference>robotalgslib/Pure Pursuit</block_reference></block_node></block_node><block_node SID="14" hasTree="0"><block_name>Utilities</block_name><block_class></block_class><block_desc></block_desc><block_path>$bdroot/Utilities</block_path><block_open>$bdroot/Utilities</block_open><block_isNotLeafBlk>1</block_isNotLeafBlk><block_position>-20   65  110  140</block_position><block_icon>Utilities.svg</block_icon><keywords></keywords><port_domains>NA.NA:0</port_domains><block_type>SubSystem</block_type><block_reference></block_reference><block_node SID="14:16" hasTree="0"><block_name>Coordinate Transformation Conversion</block_name><block_class>robotics.slcore.internal.block.CoordinateTransformationConversion</block_class><block_desc>&lt;p&gt; Convert to a specified coordinate transformation representation. &lt;/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; The input and output coordinate transformations may be specified as the representations listed below, where all vectors must be column vectors: &lt;ul&gt; &lt;li&gt;Axis-Angle (AxAng): [x y z theta]&lt;/li&gt; &lt;li&gt;Euler Angles (Eul): [z y x], [z y z], or [x y z]&lt;/li&gt; &lt;li&gt;Homogeneous Transformation (TForm): [4x4] matrix&lt;/li&gt; &lt;li&gt;Quaternion (Quat): [w x y z]&lt;/li&gt; &lt;li&gt;Rotation Matrix (RotM): [3x3] matrix&lt;/li&gt; &lt;li&gt;Translation Vector (TrVec): [x y z]&lt;/li&gt; &lt;/ul&gt; &lt;/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; Set the desired Representation parameter for both the Input and Output coordinate transformations. &lt;/p&gt; &lt;!-- convert transform transform conversion convert coordinates coordinate conversion convert coordinate transformations coordinate transformation conversion axang2quat axang2rotm axang2tform axis angle   axisangle   axangle eul2quat eul2rotm eul2tform euler ZYX   euler ZYZ   euler XYZ quat2axang quat2eul quat2rotm quat2tform rotm2axang rotm2eul rotm2quat rotm2tform tform2axang tform2eul tform2quat tform2rotm tform2trvec trvec2tform homogeneous transformation matrix --&gt;</block_desc><block_path>$bdroot/Utilities/Coordinate Transformation Conversion</block_path><block_open>$bdroot/Utilities/Coordinate Transformation Conversion</block_open><block_isNotLeafBlk>0</block_isNotLeafBlk><block_position>400  205  550  265</block_position><block_icon>Utilities/Coordinate@20@Transformation@20@Conversion.svg</block_icon><keywords></keywords><port_domains>signal.in_signal:1,signal.out_signal:1</port_domains><block_type>MATLABSystem</block_type><block_reference>robotcorelib/Coordinate Transformation Conversion</block_reference></block_node></block_node><block_node SID="22" hasTree="1"><block_name>Multisensor Positioning</block_name><block_class></block_class><block_desc></block_desc><block_path>$bdroot/Multisensor Positioning</block_path><block_open>msplib</block_open><block_isNotLeafBlk>1</block_isNotLeafBlk><block_position>-105  174   25  246</block_position><block_icon>Multisensor@20@Positioning.svg</block_icon><keywords></keywords><port_domains>NA.NA:0</port_domains><block_type>SubSystem</block_type><block_reference></block_reference></block_node></library>